CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --unwind 3
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ alive in the loop: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ destroyed once each: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [stmt.ranged]/1, [class.temporary]/6: the range-initializer
initializes `auto &&__range', and a prvalue it binds to lives until the
end of the loop.  The front end held the range in an auxiliary variable
that was never destroyed (bin53).  It is now declared, initialized from
the prvalue by the class's constructor (directly in C++17,
[dcl.init.general]/16.6.1) and destroyed after the loop.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
